Doubt related to R53 

How to Solve “Record name conflicts with another record”

You got this error because:

kopsvprofile

already exists as an NS record in GoDaddy, and DNS does not allow the same name to also be a CNAME.

Solution Options
Option 1 — Recommended (Use Route 53)

Since you already created NS delegation for:

kopsvprofile.ehmutyam.xyz

do this:

Step 1: Do NOT Create CNAME in GoDaddy

Delete or ignore the CNAME creation in GoDaddy.

Keep only the 4 NS records there.

Example in GoDaddy:

Type	Name
NS	kopsvprofile

Only NS records should exist.

Step 2: Open Route 53 Hosted Zone

Go to:

AWS Console → Route 53 → Hosted Zones

Open:

kopsvprofile.ehmutyam.xyz
Step 3: Create Record in Route 53

Click:

Create Record

Create:

Field	Value
Record Name	(leave empty)
Record Type	A
Alias	ON
Route Traffic To	Alias to Application Load Balancer
Choose Load Balancer	Select ingress ELB

Save record.

Step 4: Verify Ingress ELB

Run:

kubectl get ingress

Example:

NAME           HOSTS
vpro-ingress   kopsvprofile.ehmutyam.xyz
Step 5: Test

Open browser:

http://kopsvprofile.ehmutyam.xyz
